course: dictionary
lesson: 4949
title: Improve: make it better
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To improve something means to make it better. It can also mean to get better yourself. «A draft is a version of your writing that you plan to improve.» A draft is not finished yet, so improve here means make it better.
explain: Look at the words around improve to see which meaning fits. «Her reading improved over the term» means she got better at reading. Editing means improving the writing, with a stronger word, a clearer order or a missing sentence.
explain: Proofreading is different. It means hunting small slips such as spelling and punctuation. «A low mark can feel unfair, but feedback means advice on what to improve, and asking for it helps.» Feedback shows you where there is room for improvement.
fact: Improve means to make something better, or to get better.
fact: Improvement is the noun: «room for improvement» means there is still a way to get better.
fact: «Improve on» means to do better than before.
fact: Editing means improving writing; proofreading means hunting small slips like spelling and punctuation.
exercise: «A draft is a version of your writing that you plan to improve.» What does improve mean here? | *Make it better | Copy it out neatly | Throw it away | Read it aloud quietly
exercise: Ellie says, «Your spelling has improved.» What does it tell her? | *Her spelling is now better than before | Her spelling is exactly the same | Her spelling is now worse | Her spelling is a new subject
exercise: Which word is the noun for the action of improving? | improving | *improvement | improves | improved
test: «A low mark on work you were proud of can feel unfair; feedback means advice on what to improve, and asking for it helps.» What is feedback? | Something you only hear from friends | A kind of paper | *Advice on what to improve | A mark out of ten
test: Which sentence means someone got better? | *Her reading improved over the term | She wrote a letter to her teacher | The shop is open on Sunday | The book was sold out
exam: Editing means improving the writing, while proofreading means hunting what? | The names of the teachers | How long the lesson lasts | The colour of the paper | *Small slips like spelling and punctuation
